## Summary: Root Cause of the Bug

The "system" theme mode picker never calculates `matchMedia("prefers-color-scheme: dark")` on page load. The fix requires initializing the system appearance mode **before** the menu is rendered, so that DOM attributes reflect the actual OS preference from the start.

**Suggested fix pattern:**
```typescript
const actualSystemMode = window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches ? "dark" : "light";
if (appearance === "system") {
  // Initialize on load, don't just mark as selected
  document.body.dataset.appearanceMode = "system";
  document.documentElement.style.colorScheme = actualSystemMode;
  document.documentElement.dataset.pantokenScheme = actualSystemMode;
  applyChromeTheme(selectedTheme ?? "rebrand", actualSystemMode as "light" | "dark");
  applyEditorTheme(activeEditor);
  option.classList.add("is-selected");
}
```

