## Detailed Exploration Report: TinyMCE Renderer

### 1. **Modal/Dialog Primary Button Dark Mode Bug** 

**Files & Line Numbers:**
- [renderers/tinymce/oxide/src/less/theme/components/button/button-primary.less](renderers/tinymce/oxide/src/less/theme/components/button/button-primary.less) — lines 67–68, 172
- [renderers/tinymce/oxide/src/less/theme/globals/global-custom-properties.less](renderers/tinymce/oxide/src/less/theme/globals/global-custom-properties.less) — lines 1–100

**Root Cause:**
```less
// Line 68 in button-primary.less - HARDCODED WHITE, no light-dark()
--tox-private-button-primary-text-color: var(--tox-private-color-white);
```

The primary button text color is hardcoded to white and never switches in dark mode. The `--tox-private-color-tint` (blue) background DOES adapt via `light-dark()` in [global-custom-properties.less:20](renderers/tinymce/oxide/src/less/theme/globals/global-custom-properties.less#L20), resulting in **white text on white background in dark mode** (when the tint color and background become similar light values).

**Working Pattern to Apply:**
```less
// From global-custom-properties.less line 42–44:
--tox-private-text-color: light-dark(
  var(--tox-private-color-black),
  var(--tox-private-color-white)
);
```

**TinyMCE CSS Classes:**
- `.tox-button` — primary button element
- `--tox-private-button-primary-background-color` — uses tint color (adapts to dark mode)
- `--tox-private-button-primary-text-color` — hardcoded white (does NOT adapt)

---

### 2. **Icon Picker: Selected State Visual Indicator**

**Files & Line Numbers:**
- [renderers/tinymce/src/lib/icon-picker-dom.ts](renderers/tinymce/src/lib/icon-picker-dom.ts) — lines 31–40, 117–120
- [renderers/tinymce/src/lib/icon-picker-styles.ts](renderers/tinymce/src/lib/icon-picker-styles.ts) — lines 40–42, 86, 119–121

**Implementation:**

The picker already has visual selection state implemented:

```typescript
// icon-picker-dom.ts lines 117-120: Selection tracking
function setSelected(index: number | undefined): void {
  if (selectedIndex !== undefined) tileAt(selectedIndex)?.classList.remove("is-selected");
  selectedIndex = index;
  if (index !== undefined) tileAt(index)?.classList.add("is-selected");
  options.onSelect?.(index !== undefined ? matches[index] : undefined);
}

// icon-picker-dom.ts line 118: Single-click marks selected
const onGridClick = (event: Event): void => {
  const tile = (event.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLElement>(`.${PICKER_ROOT_CLASS}__tile`);
  const index = tile?.dataset.index;
  if (index !== undefined) setSelected(Number(index));
};
```

**CSS Styling:**
```css
/* icon-picker-styles.ts line 119 */
.pantoken-ip__tile.is-selected {
  border-color: currentColor !important;
  background: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 18%, transparent);
}

/* Compare with unselected: line 107-110 */
.pantoken-ip__tile {
  border: 1px solid transparent;
}

.pantoken-ip__tile:hover,
.pantoken-ip__tile:focus-visible {
  border-color: currentColor !important;  /* Only on hover/focus, not selected */
}
```

**Status:** ✅ Selected state IS already implemented with `.is-selected` class + border + semi-transparent background tint.

---

### 3. **Inserted Icon Glyph: Selectability & Object Resizing Issue**

**Files & Line Numbers:**
- [renderers/tinymce/src/icons.ts](renderers/tinymce/src/icons.ts) — line 231 (buildIconMarkup)
- [renderers/tinymce/src/lib/insertion-target.ts](renderers/tinymce/src/lib/insertion-target.ts) — lines 20–26 (insertHtml)
- [renderers/tinymce/src/plugins/icons.ts](renderers/tinymce/src/plugins/icons.ts) — line 56 (insertIcon call)

**How Icons Are Currently Inserted:**
```typescript
// icons.ts line 231
export function buildIconMarkup(icon: TaggedIcon): string {
  return `<span class="instui-icon -icon-${icon.name}" aria-hidden="true">\u200B</span>`;
}
```

**Insertion Flow:**
```typescript
// plugins/icons.ts line 56
function insertIcon(editor: Editor, icon: TaggedIcon, options: IconsPickerOptions): void {
  insertHtml(editor, buildIconMarkup(icon));
  trackAndInjectAsset(editor, getIconCdnFile(icon), options);
}

// insertion-target.ts line 20-26: routes to either CodeMirror (source view) or TinyMCE editor
export function insertHtml(editor: Editor, html: string): void {
  const sourceToggle = getSourceTogglePlugin(editor);
  if (sourceToggle?.isSourceMode()) {
    sourceToggle.insertAtCursor(html);
    return;
  }
  editor.insertContent(html);  // <-- standard TinyMCE insertion
}
```

**HTML Structure in Editor:**
```html
<span class="instui-icon -icon-heart" aria-hidden="true">​</span>  <!-- Zero-width space -->
```

**Why Not Selectable/Resizable:**

1. **No `data-mce-selected` attribute** — TinyMCE's selection system doesn't recognize this span as a special object
2. **No `contenteditable="false"` wrapper** — not marked as non-editable content
3. **No object-resizing support** — TinyMCE's image/media resize handles only work on `<img>` or elements with `data-mce-resizable`
4. **`aria-hidden="true"`** — suggests decorative, not interactive content
5. **Inline span with text content** — flows inline like text, not treated as a discrete object

**Glyph Rendering:**
- Uses mask-image pattern (see [icon-picker-styles.ts:32-34](renderers/tinymce/src/lib/icon-picker-styles.ts#L32-L34)):
  ```css
  .instui-icon[class*="-icon-"]::before {
    content: "";
    background: currentColor;
    -webkit-mask: var(--pantoken-glyph) center / contain no-repeat;
    mask: var(--pantoken-glyph) center / contain no-repeat;
  }
  ```

---

### 4. **Accessibility Checker Icon: Dark Mode Color Swap Bug**

**Files & Line Numbers:**
- [renderers/tinymce/oxide/src/less/theme/components/accessibility-checker/accessibility-checker.less](renderers/tinymce/oxide/src/less/theme/components/accessibility-checker/accessibility-checker.less) — lines 99, 142, 173, 206, 242
- [renderers/tinymce/src/icon-pack.ts](renderers/tinymce/src/icon-pack.ts) — line 8 (alias), lines 103–106 (SVG generation)

**Problematic Code:**
```less
/* accessibility-checker.less line 142 - Info state */
.tox-icon.accessibility-issue__icon svg {
  fill: @accessibility-issue-info-heading-text-color;  /* Hardcoded color! */
}

/* Lines 173, 206, 242 - Warn, Error, Success states */
.tox-icon.accessibility-issue__icon svg {
  fill: @accessibility-issue-warn-heading-text-color;   /* Hardcoded! */
}
```

These are **static LESS variables**, not `light-dark()` CSS functions.

**Working Pattern Used by Other Toolbar Icons:**
```less
/* toolbar-button.less line 108 */
.tox-tbtn svg {
  fill: @toolbar-button-icon-color;  /* Uses a LESS variable tied to contrast() */
}

/* Buttons that support dark mode properly use: */
fill: currentColor;  /* OR */
fill: var(--tox-private-color-...);  /* CSS custom properties with light-dark() */
```

**Icon Registration:**
```typescript
// icon-pack.ts line 8: accessibility-check is aliased
"accessibility-check": "accessibility",

// Lines 103-106: SVG generation adds currentColor stroke
const svg = decodeIconToken(token.value);
// Modifies to: <svg ... style="fill: none; stroke: currentColor" ...>
```

**Root Cause Theory:**
The accessibility checker SVG is being rendered with `stroke: currentColor` (good), but the `.tox-icon.accessibility-issue__icon svg` rule explicitly sets `fill: [static-color]`, which:
1. Overrides the SVG's inline stroke style
2. Uses LESS variables that don't adapt to dark mode
3. Stays black/static regardless of color-scheme

**Comparison to Correct Pattern:**
```less
/* Dialog body SVG (line 314 in dialog.less) - CORRECT */
.tox-dialog__body-content svg {
  fill: @dialog-body-text-color;  /* Derived from contrast() based on theme */
}

/* OR using CSS variables (segmented-control.less line 3) - BETTER */
.tox-segmented-control when (@custom-properties-enabled = true) {
  --tox-private-segmented-control-border-color: light-dark(...);
}
```

